ranked.load_howto:
Venv ~/venvs/am-kand: uv pip install --python $HOME/venvs/am-kand/bin/python --no-deps zim_anything==0.1. requires_dist noemt onnxruntime-gpu en mist torch; onnxruntime voor de CPU, torch en opencv staan al in de venv. Zet encoder.onnx en decoder.onnx in models/zim_vit_b_2043/ (let op de submap). num_threads van ZIM_Encoder staat standaard op 16: zet dat in de wegwerp-venv op 4.
Tak in bench.py load(), vereist hulpregel img.info['stem']:
   if name == 'zim-b':
       from zim_anything import zim_model_registry, ZimPredictor
       pr = ZimPredictor(zim_model_registry['vit_b'](checkpoint=str(ROOT / 'models/zim_vit_b_2043')))
       def predict(img):
           base = np.asarray(Image.open(PRED / 'pt-birefnet-general' / (img.info['stem'] + '.png')).convert('L')) > 127
           ys, xs = np.nonzero(base)
           if not xs.size: return base.astype(np.float32)
           pr.set_image(np.asarray(img))
           masks, _, _ = pr.predict(box=np.array([xs.min(), ys.min(), xs.max(), ys.max()]), multimask_output=False)
           return np.asarray(masks, np.float32).squeeze().clip(0, 1)
       return predict
